<opsproc code="00008947.0009001" revdate="2023-02-15T14:58:04"><title>Radio Altimeter System</title><procitem layer="1" lid="N.00008947.0009001.001"><title>Flight preparation/limitations</title><procbody lid="N.00008947.0009001.002"><limit layer="1" lid="N.00008947.0009001.003"><lit-limit lid="N.00008947.0009001.004">For aircraft with the <abb>RNP</abb> <abb>AR</abb> capability, <abb>RNP</abb> <abb>AR</abb> operations are not permitted.</lit-limit></limit><limit layer="1" lid="N.00008947.0009001.005"><lit-limit lid="N.00008947.0009001.006">Maximum landing capability is CAT 2.</lit-limit></limit><inform layer="1" lid="N.00008947.0009001.007"><para code="00008947.0009001.003" layer="1" lid="N.00008947.0009001.008">The F/CTL <emph bold="false" italic="false" overline="false" sub="false" sup="false" underline="true">MAINTENANCE</emph> message is displayed on the <tech-label type="s-page">STATUS</tech-label>.</para></inform></procbody></procitem><procitem layer="1" lid="N.00008947.0009001.009"><title>During cockpit preparation</title><procbody lid="N.00008947.0009001.010"><ex-conditions lid="N.00008947.0009001.011"><condition at-any-time="false" code="00008947.0009001.004" direct="false" layer="1" lid="N.00008947.0009001.012" subtitle="false" type="cond"><intro>If <abb>RA</abb> 1 is inoperative:</intro><procbody lid="N.00008947.0009001.013"><action layer="1" lid="N.00008947.0009001.014" memory="false"><cr-action code="00008947.0009001.005"><challenge><tech-label type="cb">COM NAV/RAD
ALTM/1 (121VU K11)</tech-label></challenge><response>Pull</response></cr-action></action></procbody></condition><condition at-any-time="false" code="00008947.0009001.006" direct="false" layer="1" lid="N.00008947.0009001.015" subtitle="false" type="cond"><intro>If <abb>RA</abb> 2 is inoperative:</intro><procbody lid="N.00008947.0009001.016"><action layer="1" lid="N.00008947.0009001.017" memory="false"><cr-action code="00008947.0009001.007"><challenge><tech-label type="cb">COM NAV/RAD
ALTM/2 (121VU K12)</tech-label></challenge><response>Pull</response></cr-action></action></procbody></condition></ex-conditions></procbody></procitem><procitem layer="1" lid="N.00008947.0009001.033"><title>During descent</title><procbody lid="N.00008947.0009001.034"><condition at-any-time="false" code="00008947.0009001.012" direct="false" layer="1" lid="N.00008947.0009001.029" subtitle="false" type="cond"><intro>If <abb>RA</abb> 1 is inoperative:</intro><procbody lid="N.00008947.0009001.030"><inform layer="1" lid="N.00008947.0009001.031"><para code="00008947.0009001.013" layer="1" lid="N.00008947.0009001.032"><abb>GPWS</abb> basic mode 4 "TOO
LOW TERRAIN", or "TOO LOW GEAR", or "TOO LOW FLAPS"
alert may be unduly activated above <measure category="Altitude" show-unit="true" system="US" unit="ft">5500</measure> <abb>AGL</abb>. </para><para code="00008947.0009001.014" layer="1" lid="N.00008947.0009001.035">Disregard "TOO LOW TERRAIN",
or "TOO LOW GEAR", or "TOO LOW FLAPS" alert above
this height.</para></inform></procbody></condition></procbody></procitem><procitem layer="1" lid="N.00008947.0009001.018"><title>During approach</title><procbody lid="N.00008947.0009001.019"><action layer="1" lid="N.00008947.0009001.020" memory="false"><command code="00008947.0009001.008"><para layer="1" lid="N.00008947.0009001.021">During an <abb>ILS</abb> (or <abb>MLS</abb>, or <abb>GLS</abb>) approach with <abb>AP</abb> engaged,
the flight crew must closely monitor all primary flight parameters
and <abb>FMA</abb> indications. An early/untimely FLARE and THR IDLE
mode engagement may occur in the case of an erroneous <abb>RA</abb> height indication from the remaining <abb>RA</abb>.</para></command></action><action layer="1" lid="N.00008947.0009001.022" memory="false"><command code="00008947.0009001.009"><unlist bulltype="NDASH" code="00008947.0009001.010" layer="1" lid="N.00008947.0009001.023"><para layer="1" lid="N.00008947.0009001.024">In the event of an early/untimely
FLARE and THR IDLE mode engagement:</para><item layer="1"><para layer="1" lid="N.00008947.0009001.025">Perform a go-around
(thrust levers set to TOGA), or</para></item><item layer="1"><para layer="1" lid="N.00008947.0009001.026">Disconnect <abb>AP</abb>, set both <abb>FD</abb>s to OFF and continue the approach
using raw data or external visual references.</para></item></unlist></command></action></procbody></procitem></opsproc>